{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 57,
  "title": "Angada informs their plight to Sampaati",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga57/kishkindhasans57.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga57/kishkindhaitrans57.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Angada informs Sampaati of their plight in searching for Seetha. As a part of it, he also details the plight of Rama. He explains that Seetha is unseen even after their meticulous search, thereof they transgressed the order of Sugreeva, thereby they did not return to Kishkindha, and therefore they resorted to fast-unto-death."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे सप्त पंचाशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 57th chapter in Kishkindha Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.57.1",
      "label": "4.57.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "शोकात् भ्रष्ट स्वरम् अपि श्रुत्वा ते हरि यूथपाः |\nश्रद्दधुः न एव तत् वाक्यम् कर्मणा तस्य शन्किताः",
      "iast": "śokāt bhraṣṭa svaram api śrutvā te hari yūthapāḥ |\nśraddadhuḥ na eva tat vākyam karmaṇā tasya śankitāḥ",
      "translation": "Though Sampaati's voice is turned husky by his sadness for the demise of his brother Jataayu, the monkey commanders doubtingly disbelieved neither him nor even his words by the fact of his being an eagle intending to kill and eat up all the monkeys.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "hari yuuthapaaH",
          "iast": "hari yūthapāḥ",
          "devanagari": "हरि यूथपाः",
          "meaning": "monkey, commanders",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shokaat bhraSTa svaram api",
          "iast": "śokāt bhraṣṭa svaram api",
          "devanagari": "शोकात् भ्रष्ट स्वरं अपि",
          "meaning": "by sadness, spoiled [husky,] voiced, though",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tat vaakyam shrutvaa",
          "iast": "tat vākyam śrutvā",
          "devanagari": "तत् वाक्यं श्रुत्वा",
          "meaning": "that, word [of Sampaati,] on hearing",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tasya karmaNaa shankitaaH",
          "iast": "tasya karmaṇā śankitāḥ",
          "devanagari": "तस्य कर्मणा शन्किताः",
          "meaning": "by his [Sampaati's,] deed - fact [as a powerful eagle,] doubting",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 13
        },
        {
          "itrans": "na eva shraddadhuH",
          "iast": "na eva śraddadhuḥ",
          "devanagari": "न एव श्रद्दधुः",
          "meaning": "not, even, believed - disbelieved Sampaati.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.57.2",
      "label": "4.57.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "ते प्रायम् उपविष्टाः तु दृष्ट्वा गृध्रम् प्लवंगमाः |\nचक्रुः बुद्धिम् तदा रौद्राम् सर्वान् नः भक्षयिष्यति",
      "iast": "te prāyam upaviṣṭāḥ tu dṛṣṭvā gṛdhram plavaṅgamāḥ |\ncakruḥ buddhim tadā raudrām sarvān naḥ bhakṣayiṣyati",
      "translation": "On seeing the eagle those fly-jumpers who sat for fast-unto-death have become furious at the eagle thinking that, \"that eagle wishes to eat up all of us...\" Thus, the monkeys deliberated the eagle's words.",
