      "devanagari": "एताम् बुद्धिम् ततः चक्रुः सर्वे ते हरि यूथपाः |\nअवतार्य गिरेः शृंगात् गृध्रम् आह अंगदः तदा",
      "iast": "etām buddhim tataḥ cakruḥ sarve te hari yūthapāḥ |\navatārya gireḥ śṛṃgāt gṛdhram āha aṃgadaḥ tadā",
      "translation": "When all of the monkey chiefs made up their mind in this way, then some of them on going to the mountaintop brought that eagle down, and then Angada spoke to the eagle.",
